 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT directing the New York state energy research and development authority\nstudy the feasibility of creating, storing and transferring hydrogen energy to\nresidential and commercial structures",
    "basePrintNo": "S8212",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8212-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8212\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act directing the New York state energy research and development\nauthority study the feasibility of creating, storing and transferring\nhydrogen energy to residential and commercial structures\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDirecting the New York state energy research and development authority\nstudy the feasibility of creating, storing, and transferring hydrogen\nenergy to residential and commercial structures.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: For the purposes of this act, \"municipality\" shall mean any\ncity or town with a population greater than 20,000.\n\nSection 2: The New York state energy research and development authority\nis authorized and directed to study the feasibility of creating, stor-\ning, and transferring hydrogen energy to residential and commercial\nstructures in municipalities.\n\nSection 3: study to start effective immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe study is to obtain viable data for the ability of municipalities to\npower residential and commercial structures via hydrogen power.  With\nthe recent approval and financial investment of building out hydrogen\nenergy facilities. It is crucial to make sure that municipalities can\nmaximize the effectiveness of hydrogen energy in supplementing phase in\ntheir electrical grids.\n\n*Energy Value (LBMP)\n\n*Capacity Value (ICAP)\n\n*Utility Value (E)\n\n*Demand Reduction Value (DRV)\n\n*Energy Storage\n\nWith the constant rise in Utility cost, having comprehensive data to\nassist in the cost of building, storing generated power and the trans-\nferring of hydrogen power to residential neighborhoods allow for the\ncurrent set level of invest in hydrogen energy to be moved further.\nWhile also monitoring the effectiveness of each Hydrogen plant based on\nthe regions/municipality energy consumption and the ability to meet peak\ndemands.\n\nThe hydrogen study will also allow for the renewable energy source to be\na more efficient option while also giving each area the opportunity to\nfind the most functional and financially feasible form of implementation\nto strategize the most efficient standards. The mapping/study/research\n\nthat would ideally lead to wider scale standards for efficient installa-\ntion state wide.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
